  "varnames": [],
  "consts": [
   "ui/recipe_dialog.py - confirm the EXTRACTED RESULT, not the recipe.\n\nShown the first time a matrix layout is seen (cache miss + AI configured), or when\nthe \"confirm recipe\" advanced option is on. Ordinary office staff should never see\na regex. Instead they see the extracted order as a clean preview card and may fix a\nwrong field by TYPING THE CORRECT TEXT (the underlying anchor is re-synthesized from\nthe PDF automatically). They confirm, or ask the AI to re-recognize.\n\nReturns (via ``.result``):\n    * a corrected ``PoRecipe``  -> user confirmed\n    * the string ``\"RETRY\"``    -> user asked the AI to re-recognize\n    * ``None``                  -> user cancelled\n\nUI style aligns with the rest of V2: pure-gray \"deep glass\".\n\nField structure (V2.0.19.16 redesign, V2.0.19.20 layout)\n---------------------------------------------------------\nThe dialog is SCHEMA-DRIVEN and NOT per-customer. Three tiers:\n\n  Tier 1 — PO card (PurchaseOrder level):\n      * customer\n      * season, currency, price_term, payment_terms, ship_mode,\n        country_of_origin, su, delivery_date   (shared header fields, editable via entity-0 anchors/defaults)\n  Tier 2 — one Entity card per OrderEntity (so MULTIPLE destinations are each a\n          card; destination_code lives here, not at PO level):\n      * po_no, style_no, delivery_date, port_loading, port_discharge, destination_code\n  Tier 3 — Line matrix (inside each Entity card):\n      * For matrix_2axis (jeans/trousers with inseam): ONE ROW PER (COLOUR, INSEAM)\n        — Inseam column shows the per-row length (30/32/34...).  (Option A)\n      * For line_items / matrix_1axis: ONE ROW PER COLOUR.\n      * Color Code, Color Desc      -> editable (drive colour cleans)\n      * S / M / L / XL ...          -> read-only quantity cells (live sum shown in Qty)\n      * Inseam                      -> read-only (shown per row when present)\n      * 单价 / Qty / Net Amt        -> read-only, computed live\n                                      (Net Amt = Σqty × Unit Price; the export\n                                       writes the live formula =I*K anyway)\n      * 单位 SU                     -> editable, but at the ENTITY header (Tier 2),\n                                       not inside the matrix.\n\nEdits are persisted by WRITING THEM INTO THE RECIPE (never by mutating the\npreview PO, which is re-parsed after the dialog closes):\n  * PO / entity-0 header fields  -> anchors / field_defaults / cleans (self-heal)\n  * entity-i>0 header fields     -> recipe.field_overrides[\"__ent_overrides__\"]\n  * colour renames               -> cleans[\"color\"] (+ field_overrides color_edits)\n  * matrix qty/price/inseam/su   -> recipe.field_overrides[\"__line_overrides__\"]\n``apply_recipe_overrides`` (in core/models.py) consumes the structured overrides.\n",
